  "questionLabels": [],
  "question": {
    "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">r</mi><mo>=</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">k</mi><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi></mfenced></math> for a reaction, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>50</mn><mo>%</mo></math> of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi></math> is decomposed in <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>120</mn></math> minutes. The time taken for <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>90</mn><mo>%</mo></math> decomposition of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi></math> is ______ minutes.",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [],
  "correctValue": "399",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">r</mi><mo>=</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">k</mi><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi></mfenced></math></p><p>So, order of reaction <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">t</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>120</mn><mo> </mo><mi>min</mi></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">k</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>693</mn></mrow><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">t</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub></mfrac></math></p><p>For <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>90</mn><mo>%</mo></math> completion of reaction,</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>⇒</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">k</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>.303</mo></mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">t</mi></mfrac><mi>log</mi><mfenced><mfrac><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">a</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">a</mi><mo>−</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi></mrow></mfrac></mfenced><mspace linebreak=\"newline\"></mspace><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">a</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>100</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">a</mi><mo>-</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>=</mo><mn>10</mn></math></p><p>By putting the values in above equation,</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>⇒</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>.693</mo></mrow><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">t</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>.303</mo></mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">t</mi></mfrac><mi>log</mi><mfrac><mn>100</mn><mn>10</mn></mfrac></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>∴</mo><mo> </mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>399</mn><mo> </mo><mi>min</mi></math></p>",
    "image": null
  },
